    "unit": "en-u10",
    "level": "A2",
    "objective": "Form and use the Present Continuous Tense (be + verb-ing) to describe actions happening right now, temporary living situations, and ongoing household activities.",
    "presentation": {
      "explanation": "In this lesson, we explore the **Present Continuous Tense (am/is/are + verb-ing)**:\n\n1. Formation Formula:\n   - **Subject + [am / is / are] + [Verb + ing]**\n     - *I am (I'm) cleaning the kitchen.*\n     - *He / She / It is (He's / She's) cooking dinner.*\n     - *We / You / They are (We're / They're) painting the bedroom.*\n\n2. Key Usages:\n   - **Actions Happening Right Now (At the moment of speaking)**:\n     - *'Where is Sarah?' — 'She is watering the plants on the balcony.'*\n   - **Temporary Situations & Ongoing Projects**:\n     - *'We are currently renovating our bathroom this month.'*\n     - *'I am staying at a friend's flat while looking for a new place.'*\n\n3. Spelling Rules for `-ing`:\n   - Most verbs: *clean $\\rightarrow$ cleaning, wash $\\rightarrow$ washing*\n   - Verbs ending in silent `-e`: drop `e` $\\rightarrow$ *make $\\rightarrow$ making, write $\\rightarrow$ writing*\n   - One-syllable CVC verbs (Consonant-Vowel-Consonant): double final consonant $\\rightarrow$ *mop $\\rightarrow$ mopping, sit $\\rightarrow$ sitting*.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "Listen! The washing machine is running in the kitchen.",
          "reading": "listen, the washing machine is running in the kitchen",
          "translation": "Action occurring at the present moment."
        },
        {
          "target": "They are decorating their living room with new curtains this week.",
          "reading": "they are decorating their living room with new curtains this week",
          "translation": "Ongoing temporary project."
        }
      ],
      "mnemonics": [
        "BE + V-ING: Never forget the helping verb 'to be' (I am cleaning, NOT 'I cleaning')!",
        "DOUBLE THE CONSONANT IN CVC: Mop -> mopping, sit -> sitting, run -> running!",
        "DROP THE SILENT E: Make -> making, bake -> baking!"
      ],
      "culturalNotes": [
        "Home improvement ('DIY' - Do It Yourself) is a massive cultural passion in English-speaking nations, with millions spending weekends re-painting rooms, gardening, and building flat-pack furniture."
      ]
    },
