      "explanation": "Clinical Consultation Flow (GP Clinic / Primary Care):\n1. Check-In & Triage:\n   - Presenting health insurance card / NHS number.\n2. Doctor Opening & History of Present Illness (HPI):\n   - Doctor: \"Good morning! What seems to be the trouble today? What symptoms are you experiencing?\"\n   - Patient: \"Doctor, I’ve had a severe chesty cough, shortness of breath, and a 38.8°C fever for the past three days.\"\n3. Physical Examination:\n   - Doctor: \"Let’s take a look. Please sit on the exam table. Open wide and say ‚Ahhh‘... Now I’ll listen to your lungs with the stethoscope. Inhale deeply through your mouth... and exhale slowly.\"\n4. Diagnosis, Prescription & Medical Note:\n   - Doctor: \"You have a mild acute bronchitis. I will prescribe an antibiotic and a bronchodilator inhaler. I’ll also sign a sick leave certificate (fit note) for five days of bed rest. Take care!\"",
